/** The Test LLC production import, as a permanent fixture.
 *
 * This is the Yardi Voyager "Rent Roll with Lease Charges" that was imported
 * into a live org on 2026-08-12 and then audited row by row against the app.
 * The audit found the unit/lease layer perfect and the money layer wrong in
 * five separate ways, so the workbook is kept here in full: it is the only
 * fixture that exercises, together, the four shapes the small fixtures miss.
 *
 *   · SPLIT CHARGE CODES — 11 households whose rent arrives as two codes,
 *     `rntnt` (the tenant's portion) plus `rnsvchr` (a housing voucher).
 *   · A SUBSIDY-ONLY UNIT — 245, whose single charge is the voucher code, and
 *     which a positional reader therefore classified as rent while the very
 *     same code on unit 205 became "other".
 *   · A FUTURE-RESIDENTS SECTION — 16 signed-but-not-started leases listed
 *     under their own heading, on units that also appear vacant above.
 *   · A PAST-DATED MOVE-OUT — unit 242, whose move-out is 3.5 months BEFORE
 *     the as-of date and which Yardi still lists in the Current section.
 *
 * Resident names and Yardi resident ids are synthetic; every number, date,
 * unit number, charge code and structural row is byte-for-byte the source's,
 * because the totals below are the acceptance criteria and they only mean
 * something if the arithmetic is untouched.
 */
